--- the-proposal-loop tests (epic second-brain, Story 6) ---
  PASS  U1 (contract): proposals core exports parseProposalRow, a group-by-goal helper, openProposals, a proposalEntry projection, and PROPOSAL_TYPES
  PASS  U2 (AC1/AC4/AC5): parseProposalRow extracts type/goal/whyNow/passedOver/proposalId/reason/summary/happenedOn; non-proposal/malformed → null
  PASS  U3 (AC5 — open derivation): openProposals returns proposeds with NO matching decision; a decided proposal is excluded; newest-first
  PASS  U4 (AC5 — spine projection): proposalEntry projects {date,type,summary} uniformly across proposed/approved/skipped
  PASS  U5 (AC5): the group-by-goal helper buckets proposal facts by their goal slug
  PASS  S1 (ADR d6): make-proposal — route, gate, discriminated result/refusals incl. not-viable + already-open + runner-up-*
  PASS  S2 (ADR d7): approve-proposal + skip-proposal — routes, gates, results (approved/skipped), reason-required, already-decided, and NO launch/egress
  PASS  S3 (ADR d8): the Proposal concept self-bootstraps — ensureProposalConcept via create-concept + save-schema, guarded
  PASS  S4 (ADR d9): all three new writes run through the existing serializeGoalWrite mutex (not renamed)
  PASS  S5 (ADR d3 — append-only by construction): the proposal write path uses a random/nonce d-tag and NEVER regenerateJsons
  PASS  S6 (ADR d11): GET /api/brain/proposals — route, gate, returns {proposals}
  PASS  S7 (ADR d10): the goal-detail projects the proposal facts into records[]; the brain requires the proposals core
  PASS  S8 (ADR d10): the brain import surface is re-pinned to EIGHT — the story-5 seven plus lib/brain/proposals, nothing else
  PASS  S9 (ADR d12 / AC2/AC4): the Proposal-queue view renders the emphasis card, equal-weight Approve/Skip, and the inline skip-reason disabled until non-empty
  PASS  S10 (AC4/AC3/AC7): the verbatim confirmations + empty/error states appear in the Proposal view
  PASS  S11 (AC6): the Proposal view renders NO numeric score — no score/gauge/percentage/star affordance
  PASS  S12 (ADR d12 / AC2): the Proposal-queue route + owner-gated nav entry are registered
  PASS  S13 (AC7): the Proposal view carries no banned jargon and no exclamation marks
  PASS  S14 (sentinel — ADR d10): the brain module stays structurally read-only — no mutation/strfry tokens
  PASS  S15 (sentinel — house rule): no hardcoded 64-hex pubkey in the story's touched server files
  PASS  H1 (ADR d6/d8 / AC1): make-proposal self-bootstraps the concept; the proposal reads back on the queue AND the goal spine
  PASS  H2 (AC6): the queue card carries NO numeric score field — comparisons and words only
  PASS  H3 (AC1): make-proposal on a NON-VIABLE (captured) goal is refused not-viable, with NOTHING written
  PASS  H4 (AC5): a SECOND proposal for a goal that already has an open one is refused already-open
  PASS  H5 (AC1): runner-up refusals — a runner-up that is the nominee, or is non-viable, is refused with NOTHING written
  PASS  H6 (AC3 — approve + append-only): approve retires the proposal, adds an `approved` spine entry, leaves the `proposed` entry byte-unchanged
  PASS  H7 (AC5 — decided exactly once): a second decide of the same proposal is refused already-decided
  PASS  H8 (AC4 — skip requires a reason): empty reason refused; with a reason a `skipped` entry carries it and leaves the queue
  PASS  H9 (ADR d10 — merge): the goal-detail records[] merges proposal + work-record entries newest-first
  PASS  H10 (sentinel — AC7): the hygiene check stays green — creating the Proposal concept does not disturb it
  PASS  H11 (gates): host-side calls to the new surfaces are refused by their caller-class — queue read 403, the three writes 401
  PASS  R1: the brain read surfaces this story extends are still registered (goals/detail/hygiene/orient)
  PASS  R2: the byte-pinned untouchables and PUBLIC_MUTATIONS stay free of this story
