--- teach-it-what-matters tests (epic second-brain, Story 7) ---
  PASS  U1 (contract): signals core exports parseSignalRow, groupSignalsByGoal, signalEntry — and requires NOTHING (dependency-free)
  PASS  U2 (AC1/AC2/AC5): parseSignalRow extracts prefers/over/reason/judgedBy/judgedOn/framing; distinct framing tags are preserved per row; non-signal/malformed → null
  PASS  U3 (AC3 — the two-goal fan-out): groupSignalsByGoal returns the SAME record under BOTH its prefers and over keys; malformed/self-pairs are dropped
  PASS  U4 (AC3/AC6 — the ratified wording): signalEntry words each side from that goal's perspective, verbatim, reason folded when present; date = judgedOn
  PASS  S1 (ADR d6): record-priority-signal — route, gate, refusals (same-goal, goal-not-found), result recorded
  PASS  S2 (ADR d4 — no standing requirement): the signal core resolves goals but checks NO viability
  PASS  S3 (ADR d9 — sentinel): the shared write mutex survives, and the signal handler runs through it
  PASS  S4 (ADR d2 — append-only by construction): the signal write path uses a random/nonce d-tag and NEVER regenerateJsons
  PASS  S5 (ADR d8 — the framing is server-stamped): a solve-one-today framing constant exists and is never read from the request body
  PASS  S6 (ADR d7 — attribution): the signal core stamps judgedBy 'owner', a judgedOn date, and the framing
  PASS  S7 (ADR d9): the Priority Signal concept self-bootstraps — ensureSignalConcept via create-concept + save-schema, guarded
  PASS  S8 (ADR d10): the goal-detail projects signal facts into records[]; the brain requires the signals core; the import surface is re-pinned to NINE
  PASS  S9 (ADR d10 — sentinel): NO new brain route — /api/brain/signals does not exist; the goal detail is the visibility surface
  PASS  S10 (AC4 — sentinel): the signal path launches nothing, and the story-6 proposer consumes no signals
  PASS  S11 (AC6/AC3 — copy discipline): the signals core wording is jargon-free, numeral-free, exclamation-free
  PASS  S12 (ADR d14 — sentinel, zero UI diff): no brain UI file references signals — GoalDetail/App/Layout/styles carry no signal surface
  PASS  S13 (sentinel — ADR d10): the brain module stays structurally read-only — no mutation/strfry tokens
  PASS  S14 (sentinel — house rule): no hardcoded 64-hex pubkey in the story's touched server files
  PASS  H1 (AC1/AC2/AC3 — the round-trip): a signal between two NON-VIABLE goals self-bootstraps the concept and lands on BOTH spines with the ratified wording + attribution
  PASS  H2 (AC3/AC5 — reversal + append-only): B-over-A (no reason) coexists with the original; the first element is byte-unchanged; no fold without a reason
  PASS  H3 (AC1 — refusals write nothing): a goal over itself is refused same-goal; an unknown goal is refused goal-not-found
  PASS  H4 (AC4 — recorded, never acted on): a repeat of the same pair succeeds (the corpus accumulates) and the proposals queue is untouched
  PASS  H5 (ADR d10 — merge): the goal-detail records[] merges work-record + signal entries newest-first on one spine
  PASS  H6 (gates): host-side POST record-priority-signal is 401'd; /api/brain/signals is 404 (no route exists)
  PASS  H7 (sentinel — AC6): the hygiene check stays green — creating the Priority Signal concept does not disturb it
  PASS  R1: the brain read surfaces this story extends are still registered (goals/detail/hygiene/orient/proposals)
  PASS  R2: the byte-pinned untouchables and PUBLIC_MUTATIONS stay free of this story
